# .worktreeinclude — per-machine files Claude Code copies into each new git
# worktree it creates: `claude --worktree`, subagent worktrees (`isolation:
# worktree`), and desktop parallel sessions. Uses .gitignore syntax.
#
# HOW IT WORKS: a file is copied only if it matches a pattern here AND is
# gitignored. Tracked files are never duplicated, so listing one is a no-op —
# `.claude/settings.json` and `.claude/skills/**` already arrive with the
# checkout because they are committed.
#
# NOT processed when a `WorktreeCreate` hook replaces the default git logic;
# that hook would have to copy these itself. This repo has no such hook.
#
# THE TEST FOR ADDING A LINE: is this per-machine INPUT that a worktree cannot
# regenerate and cannot work without? Generated output does not belong here —
# see the exclusions at the bottom, every one of which is deliberate.

# Local-dev env files — required to BOOT the API. The root `dev:treasury`,
# `dev:memberA`, `dev:memberB` scripts wrap these via `dotenv -e`.
# NOT required for `npm test` or either build: no vitest config loads dotenv,
# and neither app/api nor app/web has its own .env — so a worktree that only
# runs tsc/vitest works without them.
# A glob rather than four literals, so a new member env file is picked up for
# free. `.env.dev.example` is tracked, so this line never duplicates it.
.env.dev.*

# Cloudflare Worker local-dev secrets — `wrangler dev` only. Not read by the
# Worker's own vitest suite, which gets its bindings from miniflare.
cloudflare-worker/.dev.vars


# ─── DELIBERATELY ABSENT — please don't "helpfully" add these ──────────────
#
# STATE.md
#   Generated, not input. The SessionStart hook regenerates it inside each
#   worktree on the first session, and state-snapshot writes to the worktree's
#   own root. Copying it would seed a brand-new worktree with ANOTHER
#   checkout's branch and HEAD — the precise stale-reference failure CLAUDE.md
#   already has a standing rule about ("volatile state is a query, not a
#   fact"). An absent STATE.md is obviously absent; a wrong one is not.
#
# state-snapshot.config.json
#   Hand-written Tier 2 config (chain RPC, router/Safe addresses, deploy
#   health URLs) — genuinely input, unlike STATE.md. It does not exist on this
#   machine, so there is nothing to copy and a worktree loses nothing today.
#   Left out deliberately, not overlooked. Worth revisiting if Tier 2 is ever
#   configured, since a worktree would then silently drop to the
#   "not configured" placeholder.
#
# .claude/settings.local.json
#   Permission approvals are ALREADY shared and copying them would make things
#   worse. Claude Code saves "Yes, don't ask again" to the MAIN checkout's
#   settings.local.json and applies it in the main checkout and every worktree
#   of the repository (Claude Code docs, "What worktrees share with the main
#   checkout"; needs v2.1.211+). A copy here would fork a second, divergent
#   rule set that stops receiving new approvals.
#
# node_modules/ · app/api/dist/ · app/web/dist/ · app/web/.vite
#   Built per worktree, never copied. `better-sqlite3` compiles native
#   bindings, and a copied dist/ or .vite would be a stale cache that can pass
#   a build without containing the worktree's code. Install in the worktree.
